[
    {
        "content": "<p>Would mathlib be interested in explicit bounds like  <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo separator=\"true\">;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"> 7 \\le n; 2^n \\le \\mathrm{lcm}(1,\\dots,n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7804em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8588em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mpunct\">;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">lcm</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> and if yes, in what generality.</p>",
        "id": 621076531,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788365735
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Chebyshev.two_pow_le_mul_lcmUpto#doc\">docs#Chebyshev.two_pow_le_mul_lcmUpto</a> which is close<br>\n<a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"423402\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/423402-PrimeNumberTheorem.2B/topic/Bounds.20on.20LCM.281.2E.2En.29.20in.20Mathlib/with/577890178\">#PrimeNumberTheorem+ &gt; Bounds on LCM(1..n) in Mathlib</a> </p>\n<p>Are you asking because of AKS?</p>",
        "id": 621078033,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788366042
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, I wanted to port my proof from metamath to mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 621078456,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788366124
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I want to remove the additional factor of (n+1) and instead have the hypothesis <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">7\\le n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7804em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span></p>",
        "id": 621079178,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788366274
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><em>Where</em> is your proof?</p>",
        "id": 621084940,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788367455
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I formalised the proof from Nair 1982: <a href=\"https://us.metamath.org/mpeuni/lcmineqlem.html\">https://us.metamath.org/mpeuni/lcmineqlem.html</a></p>",
        "id": 621085064,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788367483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Metamath is a remarkably weak formal proof language; the only possible manipulation in it is term rewriting. I will feed the paper proof to Aristotle and see if I can massage it into something ready for mathlib</p>",
        "id": 621086218,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788367721
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, I wouldn't port it line by line, that would be crazy <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span> I just wanted to get more practice and see if this is a worthwhile result.</p>",
        "id": 621086838,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788367844
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"282271\">@Bolton Bailey</span></p>",
        "id": 621087426,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788367975
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh yes, I have a lean formalization of this result, I can post a link if that's useful, just a sec.</p>",
        "id": 621098313,
        "sender_full_name": "Bolton Bailey",
        "timestamp": 1788370235
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here it is <a href=\"https://github.com/BoltonBailey/LcmLowerBound\">https://github.com/BoltonBailey/LcmLowerBound</a> toolchain somewhat out of date I'm afraid and a few other problems with it as well (I might try to use AI to fix), <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"725717\">@metakuntyyy</span> might want to start from scratch, but possibly this could be useful for some parts.</p>",
        "id": 621102360,
        "sender_full_name": "Bolton Bailey",
        "timestamp": 1788371010
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hnnng (Aristotle was <strong>not</strong> given Nair's proof)<br>\n<img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1217x261\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/_hI3QC0oVDNNh6aw46-bfr3h/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/_hI3QC0oVDNNh6aw46-bfr3h/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 621106113,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788371738
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Aristotle proved it but I need to go to sleep</p>",
